00:40:55.880 --> 00:40:59.120
who's talking about death
and then resurrection through Nescafe.

00:40:59.200 --> 00:41:01.120
I need branding that is...

00:41:01.200 --> 00:41:03.000
But you need from happy to happy?

00:41:03.200 --> 00:41:05.280
Well, maybe it's funny to..

00:41:05.400 --> 00:41:08.400
But it just can't be death to brand.

00:41:09.640 --> 00:41:11.280
Have a break, have a Kit Kat.

00:41:11.480 --> 00:41:12.480
Can you work with that?

00:41:12.560 --> 00:41:15.520
Oh my God. Oh my God. Uncle Jimmy!

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:17.560
I have to take a break.

00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:23.800
So we are just products

00:41:24.080 --> 00:41:28.680
and the algorithm is in charge
of matching us to the client, to the advertisers.

00:41:28.760 --> 00:41:29.680
Algorithm's like,

00:41:29.680 --> 00:41:31.880
no one knows what it is, besides like...
- Yeah.

00:41:31.960 --> 00:41:33.240
It's like a puzzle,

00:41:33.440 --> 00:41:35.720
and when you get close to working it out,
it changes. -Yeah.

00:41:35.800 --> 00:41:38.080
Will we reach a point where an algorithm,

00:41:38.200 --> 00:41:39.280
a code, an AI,

00:41:39.360 --> 00:41:42.880
analyzes every single frame
of your video and the audio track,

00:41:42.960 --> 00:41:44.160
Of course we will.

00:41:44.600 --> 00:41:47.040
In the middle of the mingling
algorithm orgy

00:41:47.280 --> 00:41:48.560
of YouTubers and advertisers

00:41:48.680 --> 00:41:52.240
I'm glad to see there's still
some alternative creators

00:41:52.320 --> 00:41:53.960
making different bizarre art.

00:41:54.040 --> 00:41:55.800
So this is ASMR,

00:41:56.720 --> 00:42:01.560
and it stands for Autonomous Sensory
Meridian Response.

00:42:03.880 --> 00:42:05.480
It's really soft.

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:08.160
Hi, poopsies,

00:42:08.400 --> 00:42:11.080
welcome back to another.

00:42:11.160 --> 00:42:14.360
The Most Relaxing ASMR Video.

00:42:14.640 --> 00:42:16.800
Ever Made series,

00:42:16.880 --> 00:42:19.000
part 6.

00:42:28.040 --> 00:42:30.160
So, if I will do it, you think

00:42:30.360 --> 00:42:32.160
it can help me succeed in YouTube?

00:42:32.240 --> 00:42:36.480
An ASMR video is usually watched
from start to finish

00:42:36.600 --> 00:42:39.200
because the person will want
to fall asleep too

00:42:39.280 --> 00:42:42.200
and right now the YouTube algorithm works

00:42:42.320 --> 00:42:44.520
based on how long a video is being watched

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:49.360
so if you have a 100% of watch time
on your videos

00:42:49.520 --> 00:42:51.920
it will immediately push you
to the top of the algorithm.

00:42:52.040 --> 00:42:53.400
What a disappointment.

00:42:53.520 --> 00:42:56.880
She whispers not to us
but to the algorithm.

00:42:59.400 --> 00:43:04.280
We... we actually used to be a hub
for all the weirdo children

00:43:04.360 --> 00:43:07.840
that just wanted to seek comfort

00:43:07.920 --> 00:43:10.320
and dive into their art,

00:43:10.400 --> 00:43:12.600
that nobody else out there accepted.

00:43:13.040 --> 00:43:15.320
And now it just feels like every...

00:43:15.400 --> 00:43:18.400
every third kid is in it just for the money

00:43:18.480 --> 00:43:19.840
and just for the business.

00:43:19.920 --> 00:43:20.960
Yeah.
- That's not...

00:43:21.040 --> 00:43:23.680
That's not the honest platform
I used to know.

00:43:24.360 --> 00:43:25.160
And it hurts.

00:43:32.360 --> 00:43:34.760
I like to say that there have been
four generations of YouTube,

00:43:34.840 --> 00:43:36.600
and we are in the generation

00:43:36.680 --> 00:43:39.120
that is now... grew up with YouTube

00:43:39.200 --> 00:43:40.360
as a part of their childhood,

00:43:40.440 --> 00:43:41.960
NewTubers, I'm calling them.

00:43:42.040 --> 00:43:44.520
They saw the success of Pewdiepie
making his millions.

00:43:45.160 --> 00:43:47.480
Remember to subscribe
if you haven't already.

00:43:47.560 --> 00:43:51.480
They saw how these platforms
can be star-makers

00:43:51.560 --> 00:43:53.360
and now they're seeing it
as their opportunity

00:43:53.440 --> 00:43:56.240
to launch their own personal brand
or their business.

00:43:56.560 --> 00:44:00.640
Nasim the radical vegan, already knew
which side YouTube's bread was buttered.

00:44:00.760 --> 00:44:03.760
People like me are not good
for big businesses.

00:44:04.200 --> 00:44:05.880
The generation that was born to sell.

00:44:06.600 --> 00:44:07.680
The "NewTubers".

00:44:07.960 --> 00:44:11.000
Do you want a big company
to contact you and...?

00:44:11.080 --> 00:44:11.960
Amen.

00:44:12.080 --> 00:44:14.840
A hair-coloring or hair-gel company.

00:44:14.920 --> 00:44:17.560
My dream is to with a company
or work for a company,

00:44:17.640 --> 00:44:19.680
for a company to think I'm special.

00:44:19.760 --> 00:44:21.480
For someone to say:
Wow,

00:44:21.560 --> 00:44:23.840
he's a YouTuber,
we want to work with him.

00:44:23.960 --> 00:44:26.760
It's always nice to see highly motivated kids

00:44:26.920 --> 00:44:29.480
I'm a gamer and a vlogger

00:44:29.720 --> 00:44:32.920
and I break into houses

00:44:33.160 --> 00:44:34.400
and do extreme.

00:44:34.880 --> 00:44:36.520
What do you mean, break into houses?

00:44:36.600 --> 00:44:37.840
I break into houses.

00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:39.600
I hop the fence,

00:44:39.680 --> 00:44:41.440
my friend goes inside the house

00:44:41.520 --> 00:44:42.680
and I film him from outside.

00:44:42.760 --> 00:44:45.800
Would you get more views
if you killed someone?

00:44:45.920 --> 00:44:46.720
No.

00:44:46.840 --> 00:44:48.520
No?
- I'd get a lot of views,

00:44:48.600 --> 00:44:52.320
but I'd also get a lot of unlike
and unsubscribes.

00:44:53.440 --> 00:44:57.600
Even the convention's organizers weren't
comfortable about the net's effect on kids.

00:44:58.080 --> 00:44:59.640
So they brought an expert.

00:45:00.280 --> 00:45:06.800
So I have the pleasure of running
the largest center in the world of its kind.

00:45:06.920 --> 00:45:09.520
Focusing on the relationship
between young people and the media.

00:45:09.600 --> 00:45:13.440
We want to focus a lot on
the positive effects of media.

00:45:13.520 --> 00:45:15.120
So let's keep that in mind

00:45:15.200 --> 00:45:18.160
as where we want to go
in the next 40 to 45 minutes.

00:45:18.240 --> 00:45:20.360
Focus only on the positive,

00:45:20.560 --> 00:45:23.040
a great start for a balanced
academic discussion.

00:45:23.120 --> 00:45:27.280
We definitely see so many incredible
opportunities of media for young kids.

00:45:27.360 --> 00:45:28.360
So I've seen effects on...

00:45:28.440 --> 00:45:31.600
Positive effects on literacy, language,

00:45:31.680 --> 00:45:34.280
math, science, engineering...

00:45:34.560 --> 00:45:35.760
So we can all relax.

00:45:36.200 --> 00:45:38.200
Our children can surf as long as they want,

00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:40.360
it will make them successful.

00:45:40.800 --> 00:45:42.440
It's scientifically proven.

00:45:42.800 --> 00:45:44.800
It's okay, like, the situation?

00:45:44.880 --> 00:45:48.320
Yeah, it's not...
It's not nearly as problematic

00:45:48.400 --> 00:45:50.480
as our popular rhetoric or our media...

00:45:50.600 --> 00:45:53.240
our general lay conversation might suggest.

00:45:53.320 --> 00:45:55.240
A little too convenient.

00:45:55.560 --> 00:45:58.240
I felt as if I'm talking with YouTube's CEO.

00:45:58.440 --> 00:45:59.920
So I ask her about it.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:02.160
How much time are you the manager
of the place?

00:46:02.400 --> 00:46:05.200
About four years, I guess,
as the director of this particular center.

00:46:05.320 --> 00:46:07.800
And in these four years,
you had some partnership

00:46:07.880 --> 00:46:10.360
or some funding from...?
- I've done some collaborative work,

00:46:10.440 --> 00:46:12.400
and in those cases...
- With which companies?

00:46:12.640 --> 00:46:14.520
I would not talk about them on air,

00:46:14.600 --> 00:46:18.040
because I don't want to cause any problems
for any of my companies.

00:46:18.760 --> 00:46:20.520
I will never find out the real story.

00:46:20.920 --> 00:46:22.680
Because just after our talk,

00:46:22.960 --> 00:46:25.080
the festival's director
kicked me out

00:46:25.280 --> 00:46:28.320
claiming that I was asking
unprofessional questions.

00:46:43.360 --> 00:46:46.560
The moment I asked a critical question,
I was kicked out.

00:46:51.160 --> 00:46:54.320
Apparently on YouTube it was happening
on a much larger scale.

00:46:54.800 --> 00:46:57.240
YouTube advertiser boycotts started
about five days ago

00:46:57.320 --> 00:47:00.000
after some ads from big corporations

00:47:00.080 --> 00:47:02.160
showed up in front of inappropriate content.

00:47:02.240 --> 00:47:04.680
But the reaction has been countless
advertisers

00:47:04.760 --> 00:47:08.280
threatening to or actually pulling out
their money from YouTube.

00:47:08.720 --> 00:47:10.720
Hundreds of the largest companies,

00:47:10.800 --> 00:47:12.600
from Coca-Cola to Mercedes,

00:47:12.720 --> 00:47:15.600
have threatened to boycott YouTube
in response to the fact

00:47:15.680 --> 00:47:17.480
that YouTube has put their commercials

00:47:17.560 --> 00:47:19.800
next to violent
and racist content

00:47:19.920 --> 00:47:21.560
like ISIS videos.

00:47:22.160 --> 00:47:24.560
So YouTube decided to play it safe.

00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:27.720
They stopped showing ads,
not only in ISIS videos,

00:47:28.000 --> 00:47:29.400
but in many videos,

00:47:29.480 --> 00:47:31.920
millions, that were out of consensus,

00:47:32.200 --> 00:47:33.160
not pleasant,

00:47:33.520 --> 00:47:36.760
that the algorithm profiled
as not brand-friendly.

00:47:37.760 --> 00:47:40.080
As you know, the past year we have been hit

00:47:40.160 --> 00:47:43.680
with YouTube's mass demonetization
of LGBT channels.

00:47:43.760 --> 00:47:44.520
So we got engaged

00:47:44.600 --> 00:47:46.640
and we're obviously super excited about it.

00:47:46.720 --> 00:47:47.600
We uploaded the video

00:47:47.680 --> 00:47:50.720
and within two minutes the video
was demonetized.

00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:53.000
We couldn't figure out why,
the video is pretty PG,

00:47:53.080 --> 00:47:56.120
except that it said "future wives"
in the title,

00:47:56.200 --> 00:47:57.720
or maybe it was because two women.

00:47:57.800 --> 00:47:58.880
YouTube, what the fuck?

00:47:58.960 --> 00:47:59.960
Then we went through other videos

00:48:00.040 --> 00:48:01.720
and I found out there was like
a hundred of our videos

00:48:01.800 --> 00:48:03.400
that were demonetized
for really ridiculous reasons.

00:48:04.400 --> 00:48:07.480
One of our videos, our "Proud To Love" video

00:48:07.760 --> 00:48:10.560
that YouTube actually reached out to us
about four years ago...

00:48:10.640 --> 00:48:11.800
To make the video.

00:48:11.880 --> 00:48:14.840
In an email and said we would love for you
to make this video,

00:48:14.920 --> 00:48:17.200
showing what it's like to love
another woman.

00:48:17.280 --> 00:48:19.240
And now YouTube has demonetized it

00:48:19.320 --> 00:48:21.160
for we don't know what the reason is.

00:48:21.240 --> 00:48:23.320
What they do is they look at the title,

00:48:23.400 --> 00:48:24.520
they look at the thumbnail,

00:48:24.640 --> 00:48:28.520
and they say:
Is this even remotely, whatsoever,

00:48:29.080 --> 00:48:31.280
something that could potentially
be problematic.

00:48:31.360 --> 00:48:33.520
As a comedy satire channel,

00:48:33.600 --> 00:48:35.240
why am I getting killed?

00:48:35.640 --> 00:48:37.960
Why we removed our Wall Street Journal video?

00:48:38.560 --> 00:48:40.240
Political, no money.

00:48:40.320 --> 00:48:41.640
Is YouTube over?

00:48:41.760 --> 00:48:44.160
About the Wall Street Journal -
political, no money.

00:48:44.240 --> 00:48:47.040
Muslim edition about religion -
controversial.

00:48:47.120 --> 00:48:50.160
Very controversial,
not ad-friendly, demonetize.

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:52.560
Smile more and be happy,

00:48:52.640 --> 00:48:54.520
just don't express your opinions, guys.

00:48:54.640 --> 00:48:56.080
YouTube became the Big Brother

00:48:56.240 --> 00:48:59.480
who oversees and overhears everything.

00:48:59.680 --> 00:49:01.960
Don't talk about being g-a-y.

00:49:02.440 --> 00:49:06.840
Don't talk about being r-e-l-i-g-i-o-u-s.

00:49:07.200 --> 00:49:08.440
Don't talk about

00:49:09.280 --> 00:49:11.120
p-o-l-i-t...

00:49:13.960 --> 00:49:15.120
politics.

00:49:15.200 --> 00:49:17.880
Never talk about your own belief,

00:49:18.160 --> 00:49:21.080
otherwise you will be discriminated

00:49:21.440 --> 00:49:22.880
and censored.

00:49:23.160 --> 00:49:24.680
YouTube is a political actor.

00:49:24.760 --> 00:49:25.840
It has interests,

00:49:26.040 --> 00:49:27.520
and it exercise power.

00:49:27.720 --> 00:49:29.280
There is no information that is neutral,

00:49:29.360 --> 00:49:31.480
there is no technology that is neutral.

00:49:32.080 --> 00:49:34.560
I lost revenue on half of my videos,

00:49:34.640 --> 00:49:37.760
so that's like 4,000 videos divided by two,

00:49:37.840 --> 00:49:39.840
so 2,000 videos I lost ads on,

00:49:39.960 --> 00:49:42.480
which means I just got, like, half fired.

00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:43.920
We're at a loss at this point

00:49:44.000 --> 00:49:45.320
and we just don't know what to do.

00:49:45.400 --> 00:49:46.720
They fired a lot of people.

00:49:46.800 --> 00:49:50.240
They went from having a job
to having a hobby.

00:49:50.360 --> 00:49:54.960
I have been putting all of my money
into this channel,

00:49:55.040 --> 00:49:59.080
and my survival basically
for the last five years...

00:49:59.160 --> 00:50:01.880
And I'm probably going to lose
my home because of it.

00:50:01.960 --> 00:50:08.680
So I am just beyond sad and frustrated

00:50:08.760 --> 00:50:14.200
that I could not continue
to support myself that way.

00:50:14.480 --> 00:50:17.000
It's really painful to see people
lose their jobs

00:50:17.360 --> 00:50:19.920
their home, their life's work.

00:50:20.400 --> 00:50:23.600
But I understand YouTube's decision
to please their advertisers.

00:50:24.160 --> 00:50:25.400
After all It's business.

00:50:26.240 --> 00:50:29.040
But the more I research,
the less it makes sense.

00:50:29.480 --> 00:50:32.680
YouTube not only prevented ads
like the brands asked for

00:50:33.440 --> 00:50:37.000
but hid and even deleted
millions of videos and channels.

00:50:39.280 --> 00:50:41.520
So I wanted to talk to you about a video
That YouTube took down.

00:50:41.680 --> 00:50:43.120
It was upsetting when the video got deleted.

00:50:43.160 --> 00:50:45.040
And I'm pretty sure they deleted it for a reason

00:50:45.080 --> 00:50:46.760
that was probably a misunderstanding.

00:50:46.760 --> 00:50:50.880
They age-restricted my ab workout video.

00:50:50.960 --> 00:50:51.840
Why they did that?

00:50:51.920 --> 00:50:55.560
Because this is what they are doing
to vegan activists.

00:50:55.640 --> 00:50:57.800
Does YouTube hate LGBT content creators?

00:50:59.120 --> 00:51:01.880
So if it wasn't for the advertisers,

00:51:02.880 --> 00:51:05.480
why did YouTube delete
millions of videos?

00:51:06.080 --> 00:51:08.680
Including videos documenting war crimes?

00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:12.520
In an effort to protect viewers
from violent videos,

00:51:12.600 --> 00:51:14.920
YouTube has been deleting clips and channels

00:51:15.000 --> 00:51:17.000
showing atrocities in Syria.

00:51:17.280 --> 00:51:18.280
In some cases

00:51:18.480 --> 00:51:22.840
those videos may have been the only evidence
out there of war crime.

00:51:22.920 --> 00:51:25.680
Activists worry without this video proof,

00:51:25.800 --> 00:51:28.080
crimes may go unpunished.

00:51:28.120 --> 00:51:31.200
So maybe they made their big move
to clean up YouTube

00:51:31.280 --> 00:51:35.520
from everything that distracts us from
our only destiny, consuming.

00:51:36.560 --> 00:51:39.000
You are worried about economic incentives,

00:51:39.600 --> 00:51:40.640
that's worrying.

00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:42.760
I'm worried about political incentives

00:51:43.280 --> 00:51:45.240
where particular partisan incentives

00:51:45.480 --> 00:51:47.280
are being played and we don't know that.

00:51:47.680 --> 00:51:48.960
Or is it political?

00:51:49.120 --> 00:51:51.880
Did they wipe out millions of videos
from conflict zones

00:51:52.320 --> 00:51:55.240
to show the leaders of huge markets
like China and Russia

00:51:55.440 --> 00:51:58.600
that they don't need to worry
about Russian Spring, or Chinese spring

00:51:58.680 --> 00:52:00.360
happening in YouTube ever again?

00:52:00.960 --> 00:52:02.800
The revolution will not be YouTubized

00:52:03.200 --> 00:52:06.600
I literally can't put into words
how angry I am.

00:52:06.680 --> 00:52:08.400
This is Bullshit.

00:52:08.520 --> 00:52:10.960
What is certain
is that they made this huge move

00:52:11.040 --> 00:52:13.800
without providing explanations
to the public,

00:52:13.960 --> 00:52:15.320
to the millions of YouTubers

00:52:15.400 --> 00:52:18.240
who woke up to discover that
their lifework was ruined.

00:52:18.520 --> 00:52:20.800
I asked YouTube a direct question.

00:52:20.880 --> 00:52:23.320
I said: What do I need to do

00:52:23.560 --> 00:52:26.560
to get my channel off of your blacklist?

00:52:26.960 --> 00:52:29.160
And they sent me an automated response.

00:52:29.440 --> 00:52:33.120
And as some of you know,
I've gotten billions of views on YouTube.

00:52:33.200 --> 00:52:36.800
Okay? That equates to millions
of dollars for YouTube.

00:52:36.880 --> 00:52:40.360
I've paid lifetime salaries,
no doubt,

00:52:40.440 --> 00:52:42.960
of certain YouTube workers

00:52:43.480 --> 00:52:46.600
and they can't even give me a response

00:52:46.760 --> 00:52:48.080
that is human.

00:52:48.600 --> 00:52:51.200
Today, terror inside YouTube headquarters.

00:52:51.280 --> 00:52:52.840
We have a report of...

00:52:52.920 --> 00:52:54.160
subject with a gun.

00:52:54.240 --> 00:52:56.800
They heard 7 to 8 shots being fired.

00:52:56.880 --> 00:52:59.360
We have 4 victims, who have all been transported

00:52:59.400 --> 00:53:01.480
for gunshot related injuries.

00:53:01.600 --> 00:53:03.000
Senior law enforcement officials

00:53:03.080 --> 00:53:04.080
tell NBC News

00:53:04.160 --> 00:53:06.760
the suspect is a woman in her mid-30s.

00:53:06.840 --> 00:53:08.520
And multiple law enforcement sources

00:53:08.600 --> 00:53:09.760
tell NBC News

00:53:09.840 --> 00:53:10.760
she died at the scene.

00:53:10.840 --> 00:53:13.760
The identity of the shooter, Nasim Aghdam.

00:53:13.840 --> 00:53:15.520
She shot a man and two women

00:53:15.760 --> 00:53:17.360
before taking her own life.

00:53:17.840 --> 00:53:20.440
Growing on YouTube is not in your hands.

00:53:21.680 --> 00:53:25.040
It all depends on who is
controlling your channel.

00:53:27.720 --> 00:53:28.920
A few hours after the shooting.

00:53:29.480 --> 00:53:31.760
Nasim's videos were deleted from the web.

00:53:32.480 --> 00:53:34.960
She was wiped off collective consciousness

00:53:35.200 --> 00:53:36.800
as if she never existed.

00:53:38.200 --> 00:53:40.280
Yeah, a lot of people offer the argument

00:53:40.360 --> 00:53:42.680
that, you know, it's a private company

00:53:42.760 --> 00:53:45.480
and, you know, we shouldn't have a big say

00:53:45.560 --> 00:53:47.080
in anything that goes on.

00:53:47.520 --> 00:53:50.280
Yet at the same time
we're talking about a monopoly.

00:53:50.360 --> 00:53:52.680
People have to step in and make sure

00:53:52.760 --> 00:53:57.440
that this company isn't deciding
the fate of the entire economy

00:53:57.520 --> 00:53:59.200
or our society.

00:53:59.280 --> 00:54:00.480
And right now,

00:54:00.680 --> 00:54:05.160
YouTube is deciding the fate
of our society in many, many ways.

00:54:05.440 --> 00:54:08.320
It's a centerpiece of our society

00:54:08.400 --> 00:54:10.600
and should be treated as such,

00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:12.320
and essentially owned

00:54:12.400 --> 00:54:14.320
hence operated by...

00:54:16.880 --> 00:54:19.720
the overall community
and not just by a few people

00:54:19.800 --> 00:54:24.240
who are... working
in the best interest of a dollar.

00:54:34.240 --> 00:54:35.240
Really good.

00:54:36.480 --> 00:54:38.000
Look at these moments,

00:54:38.720 --> 00:54:40.120
all of these stories,

00:54:40.560 --> 00:54:41.440
secrets,

00:54:41.520 --> 00:54:42.600
revelations,

00:54:42.760 --> 00:54:45.000
from every corner of the world.

00:55:01.760 --> 00:55:04.520
I would have liked to tell you
that after everything that happened

00:55:04.600 --> 00:55:06.760
I took my fate into my own hands,

00:55:06.840 --> 00:55:10.360
left YouTube and took my art
back to the streets.

00:55:11.960 --> 00:55:12.760
But in real life,

00:55:13.160 --> 00:55:15.600
us YouTubers that invested many years

00:55:15.800 --> 00:55:16.760
and most of our money

00:55:17.120 --> 00:55:18.480
can't really leave YouTube.

00:55:22.640 --> 00:55:24.440
Our channel belongs to them,

00:55:24.520 --> 00:55:26.840
our subscribers are theirs to keep,

00:55:27.120 --> 00:55:29.040
we cannot take anything.

00:55:30.280 --> 00:55:32.280
YouTube is their tube.

00:55:33.400 --> 00:55:34.720
We are not citizens,

00:55:35.160 --> 00:55:37.440
we are just subjects without property,

00:55:37.960 --> 00:55:39.240
without basic rights.

00:55:42.640 --> 00:55:45.600
So until it changes
and we make YouTube great again,

00:55:46.120 --> 00:55:48.000
I'm here on the street with my gang.

00:56:01.480 --> 00:56:04.000
So my last advice is: Keep it real,

00:56:04.200 --> 00:56:05.800
unless it's depressing.

00:56:06.240 --> 00:56:07.360
Be authentic,

00:56:07.920 --> 00:56:10.440
if you're not gay or something strange,

00:56:10.760 --> 00:56:12.240
and raise your voice,

00:56:12.560 --> 00:56:14.200
unless you're Syrian.

00:56:15.280 --> 00:56:16.600
And don't be heavy.

00:56:16.640 --> 00:56:17.880
Take it easy.

00:56:18.160 --> 00:56:19.560
Buy yourself some nice stuff

00:56:20.040 --> 00:56:22.000
and everything will be okay.

00:56:27.080 --> 00:56:31.200
And if you think I'm whining about YouTube
just because I couldn't become viral,

00:56:31.640 --> 00:56:34.840
so I have a video of my son,
who can easily break the internet.

00:56:35.560 --> 00:56:40.400
But you know, the internet in the middle east
with all the wars is very weak

00:56:40.960 --> 00:56:43.840
and anyway, my computer is broken now

00:56:44.640 --> 00:56:48.880
but believe me,
it can easily get 100 million views.

